<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45233" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐσύν-θετος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>easy to compound into a
				word</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1406a36
				</span></i>
			. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τως</span>
			<i>suitably</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκλέγεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eust.
					2.22
				</span></i>
			; prob. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>PLit.Lond.</u>
				170
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>easy to put together</i> or <i>construct</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				<u>Bel.</u>
				56.34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Apollod.
				<u>Poliorc.</u>
				155.16
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of persons,
			in act. sense, <i>constructive, inventive</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς τὸ νοῆσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Man.
					5.272
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>easy to deal with</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ptol.
				<u>Tetr.</u>
				165
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
